[{:db/id 17592186064252 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9c5ee55a-541c-5782-b80c-3f5d6eae3256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c5ee55a-541c-5782-b80c-3f5d6eae3256" :question/id #uuid "9c5ee55a-541c-5782-b80c-3f5d6eae3256" :question/math-academy-id "q-15643" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=12-6x$ and the point $P(3,-6)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ determine the slope of $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ at the point $(-6,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(3,-6).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =12-6x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-6 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(3,-6)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(-6,3)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(-6) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-6))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-6)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65142116-0d83-53ff-8a22-53c3c70d6112"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65142116-0d83-53ff-8a22-53c3c70d6112" :answer-field/id #uuid "65142116-0d83-53ff-8a22-53c3c70d6112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ecb3b6c-5f9d-519e-ac19-a3e22b342ea6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ed1bca86-26ee-5bcf-a659-0ec759203aee" "answer-bc7bca2f-0e02-5b17-90a9-f17776a41ae8" "answer-3ecb3b6c-5f9d-519e-ac19-a3e22b342ea6" "answer-614852f7-d26e-56cc-93b6-f07f9c417f8d" "answer-8f042161-1e15-525d-8dc1-31568976162b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed1bca86-26ee-5bcf-a659-0ec759203aee" :answer/id #uuid "ed1bca86-26ee-5bcf-a659-0ec759203aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc7bca2f-0e02-5b17-90a9-f17776a41ae8" :answer/id #uuid "bc7bca2f-0e02-5b17-90a9-f17776a41ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ecb3b6c-5f9d-519e-ac19-a3e22b342ea6" :answer/id #uuid "3ecb3b6c-5f9d-519e-ac19-a3e22b342ea6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-614852f7-d26e-56cc-93b6-f07f9c417f8d" :answer/id #uuid "614852f7-d26e-56cc-93b6-f07f9c417f8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f042161-1e15-525d-8dc1-31568976162b" :answer/id #uuid "8f042161-1e15-525d-8dc1-31568976162b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064253 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-14d699f1-906b-5c36-8ad3-387a50daa57f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-14d699f1-906b-5c36-8ad3-387a50daa57f" :question/id #uuid "14d699f1-906b-5c36-8ad3-387a50daa57f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16098" :question/problem "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0).$\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(0)=2$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd53fe12-9eba-5b4c-ab0e-a56e97b0b5d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd53fe12-9eba-5b4c-ab0e-a56e97b0b5d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd53fe12-9eba-5b4c-ab0e-a56e97b0b5d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-59d1a2f1-8dc8-5d29-a302-08e96496fd6b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59d1a2f1-8dc8-5d29-a302-08e96496fd6b" "answer-58770571-0d16-5811-81f1-369401a6b261" "answer-ff95022d-0315-5d9e-babd-36b52f088340" "answer-bb476700-47a3-54b6-8384-b9eab15af2bb" "answer-4f3f95aa-4ff5-5778-912a-4e72354aee90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59d1a2f1-8dc8-5d29-a302-08e96496fd6b" :answer/id #uuid "59d1a2f1-8dc8-5d29-a302-08e96496fd6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58770571-0d16-5811-81f1-369401a6b261" :answer/id #uuid "58770571-0d16-5811-81f1-369401a6b261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff95022d-0315-5d9e-babd-36b52f088340" :answer/id #uuid "ff95022d-0315-5d9e-babd-36b52f088340" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb476700-47a3-54b6-8384-b9eab15af2bb" :answer/id #uuid "bb476700-47a3-54b6-8384-b9eab15af2bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f3f95aa-4ff5-5778-912a-4e72354aee90" :answer/id #uuid "4f3f95aa-4ff5-5778-912a-4e72354aee90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f566dc84-1e6c-5c3c-9fcc-e05918f8418d" :activity/id #uuid "f566dc84-1e6c-5c3c-9fcc-e05918f8418d" :activity/title "Differentiating an Inverse Function at a Point" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048441 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-b0da1a86-46b3-5c10-bca9-de55fa913cde" "step-176bf3b7-7f3b-537d-967f-47062e4a2221" "step-a496245c-b30d-521d-bb6c-1805665cc858"] :activity/f